<title>JAPAN: Japan MOF to auction two-year notes on Thursday.</title>
<headline>Japan MOF to auction two-year notes on Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Ministry of Finance (MOF) is planning to offer two-year government notes through a price-competitive auction on Thursday, a MOF official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A bond trader said the offer volume is likely to be unchanged from the previous two-year note tender at around 120 billion yen.</p>
<p>Judging from current market conditions, the coupon rate is also likely to be left unchanged at 0.6 percent, the trader said.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3-5473-3748</p>
